<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar to tender 30,000T US soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar to tender 30,000T US soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp will tender on Wednesday for a combined shipment of 18,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow corn and 12,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow soybeans, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The maximun moisture limits for the shipment are specified as 14.5 percent for the corn and 13.5 percent for the soybeans.</p>
<p>The shipment specifies shipment from the U.S. Gulf or the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Details for the tender as follows:</p>
<p>Shipment Tonne  Date/Location</p>
<p>		     U.S. Gulf	Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Soybean  12,000 Dec 1-15	 Dec 15-31</p>
<p> Corn     18,000 Dec 1-15	 Dec 15-31</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
